   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to providing\nfor a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S6416",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6416-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6416\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\nproviding for a license to sell liquor at retail for consumption on\ncertain premises\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAllows Oak & Reed, a restaurant in the City of Middletown, to obtain\na retail license for on-premises consumption despite being within 200'\nof a building occupied as a school or place of worship.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 7 of section 64 of the alcoholic beverage\ncontrol law, adding a new paragraph e-17 to allow the issuance of a\nretail license for on-premises consumption for a premises that is\nlocated within 200' of a building occupied as a school, church, syna-\ngogue, or other place of worship.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would allow the State Liquor Authority to issue a retail\nlicense for on-premises consumption to Oak & Reed, which is located\nwithin 200' of a place of worship that supports the issuance of a full\nlicense.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIncreased tax revenue\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
